<!-- SECTION 5 -->
<section id="s-transformer" data-code="transformer">
  <div class="section-no">05 — Unified Attention</div>
  <h2>Unified Causal and Bidirectional Attention</h2>
  <p>Once sensory tokens are mapped to the hidden size of 4,096, they are concatenated together with standard text tokens in the input sequence. However, they cannot all be treated identically during self-attention:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Causal Masking (Text):</strong> Text tokens can only attend to previous tokens to prevent leaks during next-token prediction.</li>
    <li><strong>Bidirectional Masking (Images &amp; Audio):</strong> Image patches and audio frames represent static physical assets where order does not imply chronological sequence (e.g., all parts of a 48x48 image are present at once). Thus, the vision and audio token blocks are masked bidirectionally—allowing elements in a single patch block or audio frame block to attend to each other in all directions.</li>
  </ul>
  
  <p>Hover over different tokens in the row of the matrix below to see the generated attention mask. Watch how the mask allows bidirectionality within modality blocks while maintaining causal constraints elsewhere.</p>

