<!-- SECTION 6 -->
<section id="s-speculative" data-code="speculative">
  <div class="section-no">06 — Speculative MTP</div>
  <h2>Speculative Multi-Token Prediction</h2>
  <p>Running a 12B model locally on a consumer laptop can be slow because of memory bandwidth limits. To solve this, Gemma 4 is <strong>speculative-ready</strong>. It includes a tiny co-trained draft module that runs speculative decoding.</p>
  <p>The draft model shares the main backbone's Key-Value (KV) cache. Since the main model's K and V weights are highly aligned, the assistant model only computes queries ($Q$) and reads the shared KV cache—bypassing the prompt evaluation stage entirely. To predict multiple tokens, Gemma 4 uses a **centroid-based classification head** that groups the 262K vocabulary into 2,048 coarse clusters before running fine token selection.</p>
  
  <p>Click "Run Speculative Decoding Step" to watch the MTP draft model predict centroids, output three draft tokens, and have them verified in parallel by the target model.</p>

